0 -15 Td /F1 13 Tf (0. Purpose and scope) Tj
0 -17 Td /F1 10 Tf (Kettleyard is the shared AI platform hub for the Tarrow University System. It gives campuses) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (and system-office programs a common way to reach hosted models without each campus standing up) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (its own identity integration, gateway, secrets handling and logging. This document describes) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (the reference architecture that every tenant is onboarded against.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf () Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (The architecture has four core building blocks:) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf () Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Tenants - an isolated slice of the platform per campus program \(namespace, quota, gateway) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  route, secrets path\).) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Identity broker - federates each campus identity provider \(IdP\) into Kettleyard.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Model gateway - the single path from tenants to upstream model providers.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Secrets vault - holds tenant API keys, client secrets and provider credentials.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (Supporting concerns: logging and redaction \(section 5\), onboarding \(section 6\), January) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (run-rate \(section 7\), open questions \(section 8\).) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf () Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (Out of scope for this document: cost allocation between campuses \(covered by the separate) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (cost-sharing model\), model selection and evaluation, and campus-run deployments.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf () Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 11 Tf () Tj
0 -15 Td /F1 13 Tf (1. Tenancy model) Tj
0 -17 Td /F1 10 Tf (A tenant is the unit of isolation, quota and accountability. Each tenant belongs to exactly one) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (campus or system-office program and has a named campus contact.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf () Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (Each tenant gets:) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf () Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• a namespace on the shared cluster \(network policies deny cross-namespace traffic by) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  default\);) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• a quota expressed as requests per minute and tokens per minute at the gateway;) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• a gateway route \(tenant-scoped base path and API key\);) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• a secrets path in the vault \(section 4\);) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• a log stream tagged with the tenant ID \(section 5\).) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (Quota enforcement \(changed in v3\). Quotas are enforced at the gateway. A tenant that exceeds) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (its quota receives HTTP 429 with a Retry-After header. In v2 quotas were advisory and enforced) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (by email, which worked exactly as well as you would expect.) Tj
ET
endstream
