0 -15 Td /F1 13 Tf (2. Identity broker) Tj
0 -17 Td /F1 10 Tf (The identity broker federates campus IdPs into Kettleyard so that tenant applications see one) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (consistent token format regardless of campus.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf () Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Protocols: SAML 2.0 and OpenID Connect inbound from campus IdPs; OIDC outbound to tenant) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  applications.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Trust: one trust relationship per campus IdP, established by exchanging signing) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  certificates. Certificates are pinned per tenant.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Group-to-role mapping \(new in v3\): each tenant maps campus IdP groups to Kettleyard roles) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  \(for example, a course-section group to the role "student" or "instructor"\). The mapping is) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  tenant-owned configuration, so a campus can change who has access without a ticket to ODS.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Service-to-service: OAuth 2.0 client-credentials tokens, scoped per tenant. Client secrets) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  live in the vault.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Session lifetime: 8 hours for interactive users, 60 minutes for service tokens.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• What the broker does not do: it does not store passwords, and it does not provision) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  accounts. Account lifecycle stays with each campus IdP.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 11 Tf () Tj
0 -15 Td /F1 13 Tf (3. Model gateway) Tj
0 -17 Td /F1 10 Tf (All tenant traffic to upstream model providers passes through the model gateway. Tenants never) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (hold provider credentials.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf () Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (Responsibilities) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf () Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• authenticate the tenant \(gateway API key plus broker token for user-attributed calls\);) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• route to the configured upstream provider and model for that tenant;) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• enforce quotas and rate limits;) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• apply the logging and redaction policy \(section 5\);) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• meter usage per tenant for the run-rate report \(section 7\).) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (Connection pooling \(changed in v3\). The gateway keeps one shared connection pool per upstream) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (provider. Each pool holds 64 persistent connections. Tenants receive a share of each pool in) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (proportion to their quota, with a floor of 4 connections per active tenant. A request is) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (assigned a free connection from the tenant's share or, if the share is full, from unused) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (capacity in the pool. When no connection is free the gateway returns HTTP 502 to the caller.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf () Tj
