0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (Rate limits. Per tenant, per minute: requests and tokens \(input plus output\). Defaults for a) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (new tenant are 600 requests per minute and 400,000 tokens per minute, adjustable on request.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (Limits are evaluated on a sliding 60-second window.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf () Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (Timeouts and retries. Upstream timeout 60 seconds for streaming responses, 30 seconds) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (otherwise. One automatic retry on connection reset, with jitter. No retries on 4xx.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf () Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (Health. Each upstream has an active health check every 15 seconds. Unhealthy upstreams are) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (taken out of rotation after three consecutive failures.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf () Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (Deployment. Three gateway replicas behind the internal load balancer, rolling updates, one) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (replica at a time.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf () Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 11 Tf () Tj
0 -15 Td /F1 13 Tf (4. Secrets vault) Tj
0 -17 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Layout \(changed in v3\): one path per tenant \(kv/tenants/tenant-id/...\) plus a platform path) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  for provider credentials that only the gateway can read.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• API keys: issued per tenant, not per application. A tenant with several applications shares) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  one gateway key and distinguishes callers through broker tokens.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Access policy: tenant administrators can read and write their own path; platform engineers) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  can write but not read tenant secrets; the gateway service account reads provider) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  credentials only.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Audit: every read and write is logged with the caller identity and kept for 400 days.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Rotation: the vault supports rotation through its API; a rotated key is accepted alongside) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  the previous key for 24 hours so that tenants can roll over without downtime.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Break-glass: two-person rule, logged and reviewed by Security & Identity.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 11 Tf () Tj
0 -15 Td /F1 13 Tf (5. Logging and redaction) Tj
0 -17 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Default \(changed in v3\): prompt and response bodies are not logged. Metadata is logged for) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  every call: tenant ID, request ID, model, token counts, latency, status code.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Body logging: a tenant may enable body logging for debugging for up to 72 hours at a time,) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  with Security & Identity approval.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Redaction: the redaction filter now runs before the log sink \(in v2 it ran after, which) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  meant unredacted bodies briefly existed in the sink buffer\). The filter removes email) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  addresses, phone numbers, student ID patterns for all four campuses and payment card) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  numbers.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Retention: metadata 13 months; debug bodies 7 days.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (• Access: tenant administrators see their own tenant's logs; platform engineers see all) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 10 Tf (  metadata, and bodies only under the break-glass procedure.) Tj
0 -14 Td /F1 11 Tf () Tj
0 -15 Td /F1 13 Tf (6. Onboarding) Tj
